XR diorama: each eye's scene scissored to the table, and each frame's own mask

For WakerQuest's diorama (mode maqueta, pc_vr_diorama.cpp) and window (patches 0026, 0030, 0033):
- The table's scissor: in the diorama's frames (the mask's fade[3] 0, the box, or 1, the bubble) the
  scene's passes in each eye get a scissor, as the window's (patch 0033), to the bounds of what the mask
  can show: the box (x and z within +-1, from the cut at y -1 to 2 m above the top) or the bubble's
  cube, and the free spheres' cubes, clipped at the eye's near plane, with the same margin. The rest of
  the room's or the island's geometry around the table (a large model crossing it is drawn whole by the
  per-object culling) is no longer shaded where the mask would hide it. Logged every 600 frames: how
  much of the eye it keeps.
- Each frame's own mask: gfx::end_frame (game thread) takes the diorama mask the frame was recorded
  with and the render worker latches it (stereo::latch_mask) before the right eye, the masks and the
  HUD. Until then (the left eye's passes, encoded as recorded) the mask in effect is read as before.
  The game thread sets the next frame's mask (its head pose) at that frame's start, while the worker
  may still encode this one: the masks and the scissors were then a frame's head move off the picture
  (the table's and the window's edges trembling with the head).

